From 642578ad64d9e6b596cd8d760769a0547607e0bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wenwen Fu <wenwfu@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] qmmf-server: activate camera server from cam-req-mgr

The normal camera server unit starts from multi-user.target and inherits the
default service dependency on sysinit.target and basic.target. This delays
camera-server startup after CAMX has registered the camera-request-manager
node.

Make the unit suitable for QuickBoot activation. The unit is wanted by the
cam-req-mgr udev add event and starts after its stable device alias becomes
active. Keep explicit shutdown ordering because DefaultDependencies=no
removes the normal service shutdown dependencies.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [QuickBoot activation is distro policy]

Signed-off-by: Wenwen Fu <wenwfu@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 qmmf-server/service/qti-cam-server-base.service.in | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/qmmf-server/service/qti-cam-server-base.service.in b/qmmf-server/service/qti-cam-server-base.service.in
index 5ecd8eb..0baccec 100644
--- a/qmmf-server/service/qti-cam-server-base.service.in
+++ b/qmmf-server/service/qti-cam-server-base.service.in
@@ -33,7 +33,10 @@
 Description= Camera Server Service
 Documentation=https://github.com/qualcomm/camera-service
 SourcePath=/usr/bin/qti-cam-server
-After=var-volatile-lib.service
+DefaultDependencies=no
+After=dev-cam_req_mgr.device
+Conflicts=shutdown.target
+Before=shutdown.target
 
 [Service]
 User=@CAM_SERVER_USER@
